{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ReaProfessor\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Live-oriented REAPER theme and script pack that aims to replace {\b LiveProfessor 2} for live sound, theatre, and broadcast plugin hosting.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER already hosts VST/VST3 (and LV2 on Linux), has deep routing, and is scriptable. ReaProfessor layers a LiveProfessor-style workflow on top:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | LiveProfessor 2 | ReaProfessor (REAPER) | | --- | --- | | Signal Chains | Tracks as chains + FX chain UI | | Wire / matrix routing | Track I/O + sends + routing matrix | | Global / plugin snapshots | ExtState snapshots + SWS snapshots | | Cue Lists | ReaProfessor Cue List panel | | MIDI / OSC / LTC | REAPER MIDI + OSC + script bridges | | View Sets | Screensets + Live Mode action | | Hardware controllers | MIDI learn / CSI / OSC maps |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Requirements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab REAPER 7.x (Linux/macOS/Windows)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sws-extension.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
SWS/S&M Extension
}}}
 (recommended)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
 (recommended)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install (ReaPack)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://github.com/JewishBidoof/reaprofessor/raw/main/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab {\b Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Import a repository\u8230 ?} \u8594 ? paste URL \u8594 ? OK\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab {\b Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Browse packages\u8230 ?} \u8594 ? filter {\b ReaProfessor} (category {\b Live}) \u8594 ? Install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab {\b Actions \u8594 ? Show action list} \u8594 ? search {\f1 ReaProfessor} \u8594 ? run {\b ReaProfessor}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Click {\b Install Extensions \u8594 ? ReaProfessor menu} (also runs automatically when the hub opens)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab {\b File \u8594 ? Quit} REAPER fully, then open it again\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 6.\tx360\tab Use {\b Extensions \u8594 ? ReaProfessor} (also added to the main toolbar)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 Pure Lua cannot hook the Extensions menu like ReaPack/SWS. The installer writes {\f1 reaper-menu.ini}, which REAPER only reads at startup \u8212- a full quit/reopen is required once.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "docs/REAPACK.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
docs/REAPACK.md
}}}
 for publishing details.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 # Install REAPER + SWS + ReaPack + JACK (Linux cloud/dev)\line
./tools/install_dev_env.sh\line
\line
# Symlink this repo into your REAPER resource path\line
./tools/link_to_reaper.sh\line
\line
# Start dummy JACK (headless / no audio interface)\line
./tools/start_jack.sh\line
\line
# Smoke-test scripting + extensions\line
./tools/smoke_test.sh\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 In REAPER: {\b Actions \u8594 ? Show action list \u8594 ? ReaScript: Load} \u8594 ?\line {\f1 Scripts/ReaProfessor/ReaProfessor.lua}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Repo layout\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 scripts/ReaProfessor/   Lua UI + show-control scripts\line
theme/                  Live-oriented color theme overlay\line
resources/              Demo project, OSC map stubs\line
tools/                  Install, link, jack, smoke tests\line
docs/                   Feature map + architecture\line
tests/                  Automated REAPER script checks\line
.cursor/                Cloud agent environment config\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Status\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Active development (v0.3.5):\par}
